import RequestProject.Wikidata.ClassAlgebra

/-!
# Disjoint union: three independent diagnostic coordinates

`Wikidata.dunOk` answers one question with one bit: is `c` the disjoint union of
`ms`, as far as this knowledge base knows?  A `false` from it is useless to an
editor, because three quite different obligations are folded into it:

* `componentsSubclass` — every member is a subclass of the holder class;
* `coverage` — every *known* instance of the holder is an instance of some
  member;
* `pairwiseDisjoint` — distinct members share no known instance.

`dunOk_iff_three` factors the checker into exactly these three coordinates, and
`isDisjointUnion_iff_three` does the same for the declarative reading.  The
three witnesses `missingSubclassEdge`, `nonExhaustive` and `overlappingMembers`
then prove the coordinates *independent*: each knowledge base fails exactly one
of them and satisfies the other two, so no two of the coordinates entail the
third (`three_coordinates_independent`).

The coverage coordinate carries an extra caveat, which
`coverage_not_monotone_under_growth` makes precise: coverage is scoped to the
*known* entity carrier, so learning about a new instance of the holder class can
turn a passing disjoint union into a failing one.  Subclass membership and
pairwise disjointness of the same base are unaffected by that particular growth.
-/

/-! ### Provenance (generated by `tools/provenance.py`)

Source mix of this module's 19 declarations: 0 traced to the DASHI Agda
bridge (`chboishabba/dashi_agda` PR #555 / #581), 14 rendering the Wikidata
